  "title": "The Camouflage Coat Check",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "perception and hidden objects",
  "premise": "A coat-check attendant must find a customer’s checkerboard coat, but it vanishes against the identical wall pattern. Instead of repainting anything, the attendant slides a plain screen behind the rack and every coat becomes visible; the customer had also blended into the opposite wall.",
  "hook": "Your coat is here. So are you. Probably.",
  "visible_action": "Patterned coats overlap the wall; a blank screen travels behind the rack; silhouettes emerge; customer steps away from another matching pattern.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Changing the background can reveal the subject.",
  "gate": "Demonstrate only the specific rendered contrast; do not claim universal camouflage or accessibility results.",
